gnatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7052cefb5e0dc084eae4432a7430f87cd287e3af54604631646933757a6e496e","event_uuid":"2f4c9628-1c89-4979-84e0-6156f7396299","position":{"commit_sha":"d8237f3ecb105b132748755451e7e56226173423","position":"1786773467472895001-2f4c9628-1c89-4979-84e0-6156f7396299"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"95e412d3633a3215aa8a9acfc3c8515cfc4fac41a16daa27aaacc403dd8af36f","event_uuid":"e808daf8-d370-424f-9a85-7564b8f0bc01","position":{"commit_sha":"051c61cafdbe916948fc62a0faa62b4a63d873fc","position":"1786773720474867001-e808daf8-d370-424f-9a85-7564b8f0bc01"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fc17d2970d06fc15efd7ce5c9e48c0f562940c8c90ced2d4877eb5f69e7ece41","event_uuid":"5ecb1772-2b84-4425-b3c8-db6ab3be5bc8","position":{"commit_sha":"051c61cafdbe916948fc62a0faa62b4a63d873fc","position":"1786773725902916001-5ecb1772-2b84-4425-b3c8-db6ab3be5bc8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c4d832559ae7b87c40f7950c341d7eb64cc235bba67ec2d5c3e566ccdee4a567","event_uuid":"37586caf-6048-4fa2-b9e7-d76dba15e346","position":{"commit_sha":"51688909b6ca8a7c152d8aacd2f8fecce932594a","position":"1786774369231458001-37586caf-6048-4fa2-b9e7-d76dba15e346"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation started in worktree tapeworm-impl. Surveyed all in-scope seams: _REGISTRY leaves (comment/tag/untag/archive/set-verify-commands), _ARGV_REGISTRY (create/idea/edit/link/unlink/revert/set-file-impact/attach-commits/session-log), lifecycle (transition/claim/reopen). Notable consumer found: rebar_reconciler/conflict_bug_filing.py parses 'rebar create' stdout via lines[-1] — will switch it to --output json as part of the normalization (invariants.py's regex extractor is already robust). Plan: new _commands/_confirm.py (context + global-flag extraction + emit helpers), router wrapper in _cli/__init__.py before partition dispatch, per-seam outcome returns (None-returning unconsumed seams), add_dependency gains a parallel on_outcome callback (dict|None return untouched).","timestamp":1786774369231458001}],"created_at":1786750030271191001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a2ac3657-6e0a-48e2-9c64-5afc3a42a123","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"fd96-e6a0-8320-4f9b"}],"description":"## Why\nrebar's mutating verbs follow the Unix rule of silence: `link`, `unlink`, `comment`, `tag`, `edit`, `set-file-impact` exit 0 with empty stdout on success. Observed cost (2026-08-14, bug clubby-circular-halicore): success and silent idempotent no-op are indistinguishable on stdout, so agents run a second `rebar show` per mutation to verify their own write; one agent misread silent success as failure, filed a spurious bug, and retried. Modern CLI practice (clig.dev; kubectl/git/gh/terraform) confirms every state change on stdout; the confirmation belongs in the mutation's own output.\n\n## Scope\n- **IN**: `_WRITES_FULL` (src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:125) + `_LIFECYCLE` (:114). Verbs that already print — `create`, `idea`, `revert`, `claim`, `session-log`, `transition` (emits `UNBLOCKED: ...` transition.py:628, `Reverted event ...` :463, though not the from->to itself) — are NORMALIZED to the same message contract (operator-approved 2026-08-14): the line keeps every datum it prints today (ids/aliases are consumed by scripts — no information loss) restated in the step-1 style, e.g. `created <alias> (<id>)`, `claimed <alias>: open -> in_progress (assignee <who>)`, Old->new mappings documented in the change + regenerated cli-reference.\n- **OUT**: MCP tools (outputSchemas already confirm), doctor/fsck/compact/bridge/tracker-maintenance (own reporting), config-key equivalent of --quiet.\n\n## Plan\n1. **Uniform message contract.** Success: one stdout line `<past-tense-verb> <args-summary>` built only from CLI args + the seam's outcome (no follow-up store read): `linked <src> -> <target> (<relation>)`, `unlinked <src> -/-> <target> (<relation>)`, `comment added to <alias>`, `tagged <alias>: +<tag>`, `untagged <alias>: -<tag>`, `edited <alias>: <field-names>` (comma-joined names of fields the invocation set, e.g. `edited x: description, priority` — names only, never values), `impact set on <alias>: <n> paths`, `archived <alias>`, `verify-commands set on <alias>: <n>`, `commits attached to <alias>: <n>`, `reopened <alias>: closed -> open`. transition's normalized line is `transitioned <alias>: <from> -> <to>; unblocked: <ids|none>` — the UNBLOCKED datum is preserved inside the line, not dropped. No-op (where the seam reports one): `no change: <specific reason>` — e.g. `no change: already linked <src> -> <target> (<relation>)`, `no change: tag <tag> already on <alias>`. Exit 0 both ways.\n2. **Per-verb outcome signal, existing contracts preserved.** Confirm each core seam's ACTUAL return contract before touching it (Serena + string grep), then extend compatibly:\n   - Seams returning `None` with no consumers gain a small outcome return (wrote/noop + detail).\n   - Seams whose return IS consumed — e.g. `add_dependency` returns `dict | None` (REDIRECT record), propagated by `link_core` and consumed by the MCP/library facade — are NOT changed; the CLI derives the confirmation from what the seam exposes, adding a parallel channel only if the existing signal cannot distinguish wrote-vs-noop, never altering the consumed value's type or meaning.\n   - Verbs with no idempotent no-op path (e.g. `comment` always writes) get success lines only; an inventory table in the change classifies each verb.\n3. **Global output flags pre-extracted at the top-level router** (src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py) BEFORE any partition dispatch — required because the positional-only `_REGISTRY` leaf verbs (comment, tag, untag, archive, set-verify-commands — `_REGISTRY` is defined in src/rebar/_commands/__init__.py:41, dispatched from the `_cli/__init__.py` router) treat any option-looking token as a usage error and never call parse_output. Pre-extraction strips BOTH global flags from argv once, uniformly for every verb (operator-approved 2026-08-14):\n   - `--quiet`/`-q`: suppresses confirmation lines only; errors/exit codes untouched.\n   - `--output <mode>`/`-o <mode>`: PROMOTED from per-verb parse_output handling to the same top-level extraction, so every in-scope verb (including `_REGISTRY` leaves) gains `--output json`. Verbs already accepting it keep identical behavior (same modes, same JSON shapes); newly-covered verbs emit ONE uniform mutation envelope — {\"outcome\": \"<verb-past>\"|\"noop\", \"subject\": <alias/edge>, \"detail\": <str>} (kubectl-Status-style; bespoke per-verb schemas are deliberately NOT designed here) — documented as pre-1.0-unstable in cli-reference. `--quiet` + `--output json` together: JSON still prints (quiet governs the text confirmation channel only).\n   Extraction is position-independent but never consumes tokens after `--` or verb-argument values (tested: a comment body containing \"--quiet\" is preserved).\n4. **Channel discipline:** confirmations print only in text mode. Under `--output json` stdout is exclusively the JSON document; the outcome rides as a structured field.\n5. **REDIRECT reconciliation:** `link` already prints a machine-readable redirect record as raw JSON to stdout on write and no-op paths (`_emit_redirect`, src/rebar/graph/_links.py:220 — an existing CLI contract), PRESERVED byte-identical; when a redirect record is printed in text mode, no additional text confirmation line is added on top (one result on stdout per invocation, no mixed text+JSON). The record is MACHINE DATA, not a confirmation line: `--quiet` never suppresses it (quiet governs only the step-1 text lines), so `link --quiet` on a redirect path still emits the record byte-identical. Under --output json the record nests as an envelope field; golden tests pin both paths.\n6. **stdout/stderr split:** confirmations to stdout (the command's result); warnings/logs stay on stderr. Exit codes unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Every verb in `_WRITES_FULL` + `_LIFECYCLE` that is silent today prints the step-1 success line on a successful write (edit's line lists exactly the field names passed on that invocation, no values); per-verb tests assert the exact line and that no additional store read/reduce builds it (call-count or monkeypatch assertion on the reduce path).\n- [ ] Every verb whose seam reports an idempotent no-op prints the `no change: ...` form, exits 0, writes no event (store-event count asserted); the change includes the inventory table classifying each verb (no-op-capable vs always-writes), and re-link of an identical active edge is among the tested no-ops.\n- [ ] Already-printing verbs (create, idea, revert, claim, session-log, transition) are normalized to the shared contract with zero information loss: for each, a test asserts the new line contains every datum the old line carried, and the change description lists each old->new mapping. reopen (silent today) gains a step-1 line.\n- [ ] link's REDIRECT record emission is byte-identical before/after on write and no-op paths, including under `--quiet` (golden tests); in text mode a redirect invocation prints exactly one stdout result (the record, no extra confirmation line).\n- [ ] transition's normalized line preserves the UNBLOCKED ids datum (test: close-with-unblock asserts ids present in the new line).\n- [ ] Consumed seam returns are unchanged: `add_dependency`'s `dict | None` REDIRECT contract and its `link_core`/facade consumers verified untouched by tests that exercise the REDIRECT path.\n- [ ] `--quiet`/`-q` AND `--output json` work on every in-scope verb including the positional-only `_REGISTRY` leaves (tested on at least comment + tag), quiet suppressing only the confirmation; under `--output json` stdout stays a single valid JSON document with the outcome field; verbs with existing --output support keep byte-identical JSON shapes (golden tests); extraction never consumes tokens after `--` or option-lookalike verb-argument values (tested with a comment body containing \"--quiet\").\n- [ ] Confirmations on stdout, logs on stderr (captured-stream tests); existing exit-code contract tests stay green.\n- [ ] docs/user-guide.md + cli-reference regenerated; `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py","reason":"stdout confirmation for comment/tag"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","reason":"stdout confirmation for link/edit"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/link_revert.py","reason":"stdout confirmation for unlink"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/__init__.py","reason":"stdout confirmation for set-file-impact"},{"path":"tests/unit/commands/","reason":"per-verb stdout confirmation tests incl. idempotent already-X notices"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e808daf8-d370-424f-9a85-7564b8f0bc01","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6bda-9d58-8546-4638","ticket_type":"task","title":"Mutating CLI verbs confirm their result on stdout (kubectl-style; already-X notices for idempotent no-ops)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c92046d3-4293-4ec0-9333-46ae38ab3473","fb0a4ee2-ba48-4816-bfc8-82a4364eb7b9","78f639fd-4ac4-4fc0-9596-c7e66befda7d","c97276b9-105b-4184-b6ff-e1f9e0c7b3f4","2d4693a5-bb2f-40f1-9cdb-7d9a0cecf38e","c51ee75c-f9eb-4b93-b9a6-931e9e9ef0f6","d6c0c22e-3412-451e-9421-727613244fc6","01794d1d-5d4b-4fdc-a6c0-bbdf26de8387","52c3c934-e40f-454a-97aa-fd66384c8ce3","f1716d20-5d8a-44dc-8828-2b0bf5525175","2f4c9628-1c89-4979-84e0-6156f7396299","e808daf8-d370-424f-9a85-7564b8f0bc01","5ecb1772-2b84-4425-b3c8-db6ab3be5bc8","37586caf-6048-4fa2-b9e7-d76dba15e346"]},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786778484715801001,"uuid":"f0cdfb2b-cba9-4b6a-801c-750ebee249f2"}